Address an outgoing call's offer to the peer's primary phone only.

Origin: fazer-ai/whatsapp-connector, not upstream.

Why: when the peer has WhatsApp Desktop (or Web) open, that companion preaccepts first,
and after the phone answers no audio from the phone ever reaches us. Sending the offer
and the encrypted call key to device 0 alone keeps the companion out of the call, and
audio then flows both ways. The same failure reproduces with oxidezap/whatsapp-rust, so
it is not a meowcaller defect we could fix in place. The cost: the peer's companion
devices do not ring for calls the connector places. Measured in
fazer-ai/whatsapp-connector#380 (comment of 2026-10-07).

diff --git a/engine.go b/engine.go
index b7684b4..f6d2ec5 100644
--- a/engine.go
+++ b/engine.go
@@ -460,6 +460,18 @@ func (e *engine) placeCall(ctx context.Context, target string, opts CallOptions)
 	if len(devices) == 0 {
 		return nil, fmt.Errorf("peer %s has no devices (unreachable / not on WhatsApp)", peerLID)
 	}
+	// Ring only the peer's primary phone. When a companion device (WhatsApp Desktop,
+	// Web) is online it preaccepts first and, once the phone answers, the phone's media
+	// never reaches our relays. A peer without device 0 listed keeps the old fanout.
+	primary := devices[:0:0]
+	for _, d := range devices {
+		if d.Device == 0 {
+			primary = append(primary, d)
+		}
+	}
+	if len(primary) > 0 {
+		devices = primary
+	}
 
 	var callKey [32]byte
